# Local ESPHome configuration and build state. The wildcard covers the private
# working source and every profile rendered from it, so a new private render
# cannot land untracked-and-unignored with real credentials in it. The two
# public profiles use the WaveshareESP32S3PhotoPainter73e6- prefix instead and
# are unaffected.
ESPHome/Office-PhotoPainter*.yaml
secrets.yaml
# ESPHome dashboard backups can hold the same credentials.
*.backup
.esphome/
build/

# Most development tooling remains local because it can render private source
# profiles or sanitize raw logs. The package verification entry point is public
# so every package consumer fixture can be rebuilt reproducibly.
scripts/*
!scripts/verify_esphome_packages.sh
!scripts/generate_esphome_profiles.py
AGENTS.md

# Locally cached third-party reference material. The published provenance and
# retrieval information lives in Documentation/README.md and References/.
Documentation/*.pdf
ESP32-S3-PhotoPainter-Demo/
PhotoPainter_B-BMP/
OpenDisplay/

# Raw, unsanitized device logs. These can contain Wi-Fi credentials, API keys,
# hostnames, and IP addresses, so they never leave the development machine.
# Sanitized copies are published under Logs/ instead.
DirtyLogs/

# OS/editor artifacts
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Local-only review notes. Generated against the private working configuration
# and referencing its line numbers, so it stays on the development machine.
FINDINGS.md

# Real credentials for a flashable build. Never committed; ensure_secrets.py
# copies it over secrets.yaml when present.
ESPHome/secrets.real.yaml
secrets.real.yaml

# Full-resolution original of the README photo; the published copy is
# Images/diagnostic-dashboard.jpg (resized, metadata stripped).
Images/IMG_1469.png
